# Test: macro-error with span-of for precise error location
#
# This test verifies that macro-error correctly uses the span from span-of
# to report errors at the exact source location of the problematic argument.

# Define a macro that validates its argument and errors with span if invalid
[macro expect-int [let arg]
  [if [int? arg]
    arg
    [macro-error [span-of arg] "expected an integer literal"]]]

# Call the macro with an invalid argument (a string instead of int)
# The error should point to the "hello" argument location
[expect-int "hello"]
=== error
[E012] macro expansion error: expected an integer literal
